{"availability":"available","full":"pal-123456789/dogfood-portal","name":"dogfood-portal","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-26T18:36:42Z","updated":"2026-09-29T17:14:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://pal-123456789.github.io/dogfood-portal/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:47.924Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:47.924Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:47.924Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:47.924Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2104986907386282130","postId":"2104986907386282130","postedAt":"2026-09-29T17:29:22.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T08:18:48.262Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hostable hackathon submission-and-judging platform. It is a single Django 5.2 + PostgreSQL 16 monolith — no Redis, no message broker, no separate worker — that boots from one command with a seeded demo event, collects submissions, runs a judging panel, normalizes scores to remove judge severity, and publishes a frozen, signed result that anyone can re-verify offline on a clean machine. Caching and rate-limit counters live in a database table (DatabaseCache) and static files are served in-process by WhiteNoise (src/portal/settings.py).","This project is graded against over-claiming, so both this file and docs/ are written to be checkable line-by-line against src/. Anything not wired to an endpoint is labelled planned in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, not described here as if it shipped."],"features":["Every bullet names the code that implements it.","Public project gallery at GET /projects, with an optional ?track= filter","(src/gallery/views.py).","Submission intake, edit and withdraw — a participant creates a submission at","POST /projects/new, which refuses writes after the event deadline, then revises or soft-withdraws it at /submissions/mine, /submissions//edit, /submissions//withdraw. Withdrawal hides the project from the gallery…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pal-123456789/dogfood-portal/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"df23eca447ef3c21d1cdede037d6ae98e469afaa69d352c70cfd44dd8d146036","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:47.924Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:47.924Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A self-hostable hackathon submission-and-judging platform. It is a single Django 5.2 + PostgreSQL 16 monolith — no Redis, no message broker, no separate worker — that boots from one command with a seeded demo event, collects submissions, runs a judging panel, normalizes scores to remove judge severity, and publishes a frozen, signed result that anyone can re-verify offline on a clean machine. Caching and rate-limit counters live in a database table (DatabaseCache) and static files are served in-process by WhiteNoise (src/portal/settings.py).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pal-123456789/dogfood-portal/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"This exists so an automated acceptance > checker can drive the app without a login flow; it is not an authentication mechanism. > Set DOGFOODDEMO=0 for any real deployment — with the flag off the shim is inert and the > ordinary login flow at /accounts/login/ applies.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pal-123456789/dogfood-portal/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Author identity is surfaced as a display name only, never the login email (src/comments/{views,services}.py).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pal-123456789/dogfood-portal/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"It is software you self-host.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pal-123456789/dogfood-portal/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"df23eca447ef3c21d1cdede037d6ae98e469